WEBVTT

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:06.740
Forming a trade alliance with Musashi?

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.240
I think that's a fairly interesting proposition, but...

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:15.080
Tres España does not approve of that alliance.

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:19.710
Why aren't you going to war with England anyway?

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:26.630
<i>Everyone, let's be honest here.</i>

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:29.680
<i>If you can think of any reason for him to say that, come clean.</i>

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:37.770
It's because of me. But why?

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:39.770
Tes. It is because of you.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:46.690
You warred against us, claiming that killing Princess Horizon was a misuse of historical reenactments.

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:53.700
Then what about England, which will execute Bloody Mary so we can start fighting with the Spanish Armada?

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.710
You seem to be holding an intriguing conversation.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:00.290
I'm going to butt in.

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.920
I am allied with P.A. ODA's P.A.O.M.

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:07.670
I am our Student Council's treasurer and have succeeded the two names:

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:11.300
No. 4 in the Five Great Peaks, Mercenary King Wallenstein

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:13.720
and Maeda Toshiie.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:53.610
Long time no see, Your Majesty.

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:54.320
Drain!

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:57.620
You want me to bow?

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:10.040
Whoa, that's rude, Macchan!

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:17.180
I am going to join in on this conversation.

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:22.060
M.H.R.R. cannot approve of your trade alliance with Musashi.

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:23.770
Is it because your nation

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:25.770
is currently in the middle of the 30 Years' War?

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:27.940
There is that,

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:31.690
but don't you see how impossible this alliance is?

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:36.570
If England and Musashi formed a trade alliance,

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:39.410
I think we'd get so pissed we'd come crush you both.

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:42.660
Should that happen, the European flight paths would turn into Hell.

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:45.910
Wouldn't that pose a problem for England?

00:03:47.170 --> 00:03:49.380
That's why I'm thinking,

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:51.420
If England can,

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:54.380
I would like them to destroy Musashi right here.

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:12.820
P.A. ODA was the only member of the Testament Union to not get an Armament of Deadly Sins.

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:17.570
So instead, our Lord bequeathed other weapons

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:20.870
unto the Five Great Peaks of the Six Tenma Armies.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:28.330
Macchan and I received "Israfel".

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:32.960
Its ability reverses the power to heal and allows me to preserve and develop one's soul.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:34.750
<i>There's so many!</i>

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:35.920
<i>There must be at least 20,000 of them.</i>

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:40.510
If necessary, I can even awaken an army of a million from the Underworld.

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:43.550
This is truly my Million Hells of Kaga.

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:46.520
Or as the M.H.R.R. calls it -

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:48.940
The Kaga Million Geists.

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:53.060
Fairy Queen, could you issue the order?

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:55.270
Tell me to destroy Musashi.

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:59.280
Is P.A. ODA turning hostile against Musashi?

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:01.110
You're such an idiot.

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:03.490
Someday we will fight in the Battle of Sekigahara,

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:05.240
so isn't it clear that we're enemies?

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:11.710
Hold it right there!

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:14.210
Rolling, rolling, rolling, rolling, rolling!

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:18.590
L-L-Lunatic!

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:20.380
Macchan, that's too strong of a fastball!

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:22.800
Yikes! That's my shirt!

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:24.260
Yay!

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:25.720
Oh, really?

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:28.560
I found it when I was naked and drinking tea in the girl's dressing room.

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:31.020
Th-The girl's dressing room?!

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:34.060
Oh, Asama! I tried yours on too!

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:35.820
You seriously have colossal tits, don't you?

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:38.690
It was all baggy and bouncy and—

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:40.280
Ah! Don't!

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:44.820
Oh?

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:48.040
You brought a weapon to our meeting?

00:05:48.830 --> 00:05:50.410
No, this isn't—

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:51.620
Your Majesty!

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:54.670
This is a tool necessary for shrine maidens to carry out ceremonies.

00:05:54.670 --> 00:05:55.590
It isn't a weapon!

00:05:55.590 --> 00:05:56.500
As evidenced by...

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:57.710
I'm back!

00:05:58.090 --> 00:05:59.380
The bath's open.

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:01.970
See how that moron is completely unscathed?

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:05.050
True, no one in Musashi is so rude

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:08.600
as to bring a weapon to an audience with—

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:20.650
Isn't that...?

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:22.240
Isn't that...?

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:28.700
<i>I-In other words, you want me to handle this?</i>

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:35.830
W-Well, you see, this may <i>look</i> like an Armament of Deadly Sins, but it isn't!

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:38.340
Uh-huh, that's a new one.

00:06:38.670 --> 00:06:41.380
This is a... body pillow!

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:43.800
Right, it's a body pillow!

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:45.430
You snuggle it like this and—

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:47.390
There's a blade! That was a close call!

00:06:50.890 --> 00:06:54.140
Ouch. Their silence is killing me.

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:55.850
<i>The poor thing...</i>

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:58.610
<i>I feel really sorry for her that this is a live national transmission.</i>

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:03.110
Hey, Musashi!

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:06.570
Quit getting all worked up and answer my question already.

00:07:07.030 --> 00:07:09.030
Aren't you going to war with them?

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:13.080
Huh? Why do we have to go to war?

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:14.910
No matter what excuse they give,

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:18.420
Mary's execution is a misuse of the Testament.

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:21.500
So you have to go to war with them,

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:23.760
just like you did for the princess over there.

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:25.930
Hey, Horizon?

00:07:25.930 --> 00:07:26.720
Judge.

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:29.180
You were the one getting saved, right?

00:07:29.180 --> 00:07:31.180
So what do you think of this affair?

00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:34.180
There is one thing I do not understand.

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:35.350
Oh, what is it?

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:39.810
Isn't executing someone who is prepared to die

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:41.860
proper use of the Testament, not misuse?

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:48.240
I can comprehend the concept that we should prevent the loss of life.

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:51.530
But if I were to give that concept one exception,

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:54.370
it would be based upon what has been
pre-determined by historical reenactments.

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:57.250
If history is accurately reproduced,

00:07:57.250 --> 00:08:01.210
that person's death will put the world on the path of continued existence.

00:08:01.670 --> 00:08:04.710
As such, if the person in question wishes to die,

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:08.970
how could you justifiably claim that promoting her death is wrong?

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:10.590
That's right.

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:12.760
You don't have any emotions, do you?

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:14.930
Judge, I'm afraid not.

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:19.310
Why would you try to interfere with what another desires?

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:20.560
Well...

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:22.150
Please answer me.

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:24.820
You would prevent what another wants.

00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:28.360
What are your criteria for determining right from wrong?

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:33.240
If I understood your criteria...

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:34.910
Should a time come when I do,

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:38.750
I would like to go to war to rescue Queen Mary.

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:40.040
Sweet!

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:43.340
Tres España, did you hear her answer just now?

00:08:43.670 --> 00:08:48.840
Tes. Her answer indicates that she fails to understand the importance of our historical reenactments.

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:52.470
But inversely, she comprehends the importance of how they are to be interpreted.

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:53.680
In which case...?

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:55.430
It is simple.

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:58.140
I shall send a report indicating that we should

00:08:58.140 --> 00:08:59.270
prepare to declare war.

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:01.440
So it's coming down to that?

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:03.360
But even so, Old Geezer!

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:06.900
Don't go deciding how someone else feels!

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:10.200
Isn't that one of the baby basics behind true love erotic games?!

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:11.570
So, y'know what?

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:12.570
What?

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:15.330
You should have more faith in Horizon here.

00:09:15.330 --> 00:09:19.790
If someone falls in love with Mary and gets Horizon to understand what that means,

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:22.790
we will definitely go save Mary!

00:09:23.130 --> 00:09:24.290
You got that?

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:26.590
We absolutely, totally, definitely will!

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:29.550
You can't let your guard down around these guys.

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:33.090
Let's put these fun and games to an end, Musashi.

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:35.550
Orders to attack, Fairy Queen.

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:38.060
You're being pushy, Maeda Toshiie.

00:09:38.850 --> 00:09:42.480
The Fairy Queen is currently holding a meeting with Musashi.

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:44.860
Realize that outsiders will be treated accordingly.

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:47.530
Who are the real outsiders here, Musashi?

00:09:48.030 --> 00:09:50.440
<i>You</i> are the outsiders in <i>our</i> history.

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:55.120
Fairy Queen, forming that trade alliance has become difficult for you.

00:09:55.570 --> 00:09:58.290
I would like to withdraw that proposition. May I?

00:09:58.290 --> 00:10:01.750
Tes. What will you give us in exchange?

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:06.130
I would like you to cancel your contract with Mercenary King Wallenstein.

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:07.380
Really now?

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:09.630
Do you know what that means?

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:16.680
By having England send my Kaga Million Geists to the front lines in the upcoming Spanish Armada battle,

00:10:16.680 --> 00:10:19.470
you would cut your own losses.

00:10:19.470 --> 00:10:24.900
If you cancel that, who will take the lead and fight against the Grande y Felicísima Armada?

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:26.560
I shall tell you.

00:10:27.110 --> 00:10:29.820
I, Honda Masazumi, Vice President

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:32.030
of Musashi Ariadust Academy, make this proposal -

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:36.410
I offer to let England use Musashi as its fleet in the Spanish Armada battle.

00:10:43.460 --> 00:10:47.130
She intends to treat Musashi as if it were a group of mercenaries?

00:10:47.130 --> 00:10:49.800
So what if she does, Former Pupil?

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:53.170
If they were hired by another country as mercenaries,

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:55.800
Musashi would be viewed as that country's navy

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:58.680
and they could obtain weaponry as a "business necessity".

00:10:59.180 --> 00:11:01.180
That's a rather convenient interpretation.

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:06.690
But that would instantly resolve the issues between England and Musashi.

00:11:07.150 --> 00:11:12.820
Maeda Toshiie, can you give your employer a better offer?

00:11:13.530 --> 00:11:15.070
I want to ask you something.

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:15.780
What?

00:11:16.280 --> 00:11:18.030
Have you ever been to Avalon?

00:11:19.370 --> 00:11:22.790
I bet you've heard of it, but have never gone there, correct?

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:28.500
Tes. That shows the value of your worth.

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:29.960
How so?!

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:32.590
You still don't know everything.

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:37.010
Around and around; you merely flew around the Far East.

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:40.260
Westphalia must feel terribly far off.

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:49.690
The Nikyou Crest?!

00:11:51.400 --> 00:11:53.070
Vice President of Musashi.

00:11:53.530 --> 00:11:54.570
Judge.

00:11:54.570 --> 00:11:57.950
I have negated my contract with the Mercenary King.

00:11:57.950 --> 00:12:00.070
Now that things have come to this, there is neither right nor wrong.

00:12:00.450 --> 00:12:03.830
I shall accept your offer to make Musashi England's fleet.

00:12:03.830 --> 00:12:05.330
Is that acceptable?

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:08.330
Judge, Fairy Queen.

00:12:08.750 --> 00:12:11.840
Then I hereby draw this evening's party to a close.

00:12:15.970 --> 00:12:19.640
Fairy Queen, I was told that you were going to take me to Avalon,

00:12:19.640 --> 00:12:21.430
but this is just behind the throne room.

00:12:21.430 --> 00:12:22.970
Is something back here?

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:23.810
Tes.

00:12:24.350 --> 00:12:26.350
I'm bringing you here because there <i>is</i> something.

00:12:27.270 --> 00:12:28.730
Why is there a hole?

00:12:28.730 --> 00:12:30.400
Let me see your head for a moment.

00:12:33.070 --> 00:12:34.860
I authorize temporary permission to enter.

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:36.240
That hurt!

00:12:36.240 --> 00:12:39.070
Not that this was a necessary part of the ritual or anything.

00:12:39.360 --> 00:12:41.240
Then why did you hit me?!

00:12:41.240 --> 00:12:42.660
I felt like it.

00:12:42.660 --> 00:12:45.240
After all, I like putting on shows.

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:46.160
Get used to it.

00:12:46.790 --> 00:12:47.790
Uh-huh...

00:12:55.050 --> 00:12:56.010
Is this...?

00:12:56.010 --> 00:12:57.720
Indeed it is. This is Avalon.

00:12:58.090 --> 00:13:00.340
Is it a Harmonic Field?

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:02.430
No, it is a compressed dimension.

00:13:03.180 --> 00:13:07.020
My father made it since his room in the Tower of London was too cramped.

00:13:07.020 --> 00:13:08.730
Chancellor Henry VIII made it?

00:13:14.900 --> 00:13:16.570
Remnants of the past?

00:13:16.570 --> 00:13:19.450
Tes. Apparently, since he compressed the ether,

00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:24.070
the actions made by ether-based entities such as ourselves remained in this space.

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:26.660
But which one is you, Fairy Queen?

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:31.920
I don't really remember which of us is which.

00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:35.420
Ether-based entities are born from the Earth Pulse,

00:13:35.420 --> 00:13:37.840
so we are connected to one another through the pulses.

00:13:37.840 --> 00:13:40.420
This is especially true of twin sisters.

00:13:41.470 --> 00:13:44.260
Back when I was a naïve child still developing a personality,

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:48.180
my personal barrier was weak and it was easy for our emotions to link.

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:49.180
Then...

00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:51.270
That link has grown weak.

00:13:51.270 --> 00:13:53.900
It has changed to the act of "trusting" each other.

00:13:54.190 --> 00:13:57.150
But that is precisely why we made a promise.

00:13:58.860 --> 00:14:02.910
It looks as if I am consoling my elder sister when she learned of her execution

00:14:02.910 --> 00:14:04.870
and my elder sister appears to be consoling me

00:14:04.870 --> 00:14:06.910
after I learned of said execution.

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:09.410
"Save you from anything".

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:12.410
What a pathetic story.

00:14:13.210 --> 00:14:17.840
In return for how my elder sister tried to protect me

00:14:17.840 --> 00:14:20.840
I can only protect her by returning her to the Earth Pulse

00:14:20.840 --> 00:14:22.760
since I must observe the historical reenactments.

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:29.680
Tes.

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:32.600
Are you familiar with "changelings"?

00:14:32.890 --> 00:14:33.940
Judge.

00:14:33.940 --> 00:14:38.360
Isn't it a form of teasing done by fairies where they swap or hide children?

00:14:38.360 --> 00:14:39.190
Meaning...?

00:14:39.530 --> 00:14:41.440
Apparently they were swapped out.

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:44.410
The Fairy Queen and Double Bloody Mary got swapped.

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:48.200
"Save you from anything".

00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:50.950
I don't know the details,

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:54.210
but there was one reenactment

00:14:54.210 --> 00:14:58.210
that Double Bloody Mary saved for the very end.

00:14:58.210 --> 00:14:59.210
Was it...?

00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:03.550
Tes. The execution of 300 members of the Anglican Church.

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:05.970
That is how "Bloody Mary" got her name.

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:10.140
She personally fought against three hundred people,

00:15:10.140 --> 00:15:12.220
was covered in scars and said,

00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:16.600
These scars are proof that Bloody Mary exists.

00:15:18.110 --> 00:15:21.940
Then Mary hid her face and was confined to the Tower of London.

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:24.700
That is when the Fairy Queen took the spotlight.

00:15:25.150 --> 00:15:27.360
This is how England has reenacted history.

00:15:27.870 --> 00:15:31.790
The Queen's past and the fate of our world can both be seen in Avalon.

00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:33.830
That is the type of place it is.

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:36.290
What do you mean by "the fate of our world"?

00:15:36.710 --> 00:15:40.920
Tes. Chancellor Henry VIII had conducted research

00:15:40.920 --> 00:15:44.130
on determining what precisely the apocalypse is. And...

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:45.510
This is the apocalypse.

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:47.680
What do you mean?

00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:49.510
Vice President of Musashi,

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:53.270
what is currently appearing in the world as it draws closer to the apocalypse?

00:15:53.600 --> 00:15:55.600
Strange phenomena and the like...

00:15:56.730 --> 00:15:59.690
Are the strange phenomena in England being compressed here?

00:16:00.190 --> 00:16:03.650
Tes. If these phenomena are occurring due to the apocalypse,

00:16:03.650 --> 00:16:05.530
then they are its small-scale versions.

00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:08.030
Or they could be the tools of the apocalypse.

00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:12.200
That's why he concentrated the warp made by the apocalypse in our Earth Pulse here.

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:13.330
Is there any proof?

00:16:13.330 --> 00:16:15.290
Tes. Try throwing something in.

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:27.340
What just happened?

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:30.640
It looked like the glove was reduced to ether.

00:16:30.640 --> 00:16:32.260
It did no such thing.

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:36.140
Using the process to turn it into ether, it eradicated the glove.

00:16:36.560 --> 00:16:39.650
It destroyed the ether, creating absolute nothingness.

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:43.070
That is what we believe the apocalypse holds.

00:16:43.400 --> 00:16:45.070
Absolute nothingness?

00:16:45.360 --> 00:16:50.360
Tes. The ether that gave that glove form has vanished from our world.

00:16:50.990 --> 00:16:53.160
It created a hole, formed a distortion,

00:16:53.160 --> 00:16:56.580
and somewhere a small-scale strange phenomenon is sure to occur.

00:16:56.580 --> 00:16:57.080
Wha—

00:16:57.080 --> 00:16:58.410
Don't worry about it.

00:16:58.870 --> 00:17:03.090
Normally the hole automatically mends itself, naturally closing back up.

00:17:03.090 --> 00:17:05.000
Then how are you keeping this hole open?

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:08.130
By overlapping the distortions, we forced the hole open.

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:10.800
We widened the surrounding Earth Pulses to maintain it.

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:16.010
Fairy Queen, is this what you consider the apocalypse?

00:17:16.390 --> 00:17:18.180
The whole world will distort

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:23.020
and the amount of nothingness created will overwhelm the Earth Pulses' ability to heal themselves?

00:17:23.020 --> 00:17:26.610
Tes. That is our consensus.

00:17:27.820 --> 00:17:29.820
Then the other countries included in that consensus...

00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:32.530
Tes. You have rather good insight.

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:40.660
That takes me back...

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:43.790
Aren't crosses forbidden by the Anglican Church?

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:46.210
Then who do you think it belonged to?

00:17:48.050 --> 00:17:49.670
"Long time, my friend".

00:17:49.970 --> 00:17:53.930
Tes. My father always said that whenever he came here.

00:17:54.470 --> 00:17:58.180
The owner of that cross was the Chancellor of Tres España

00:17:58.180 --> 00:18:03.230
and Emperor Chancellor of M.H.R.R., Chancellor Carlos I.

00:18:03.770 --> 00:18:07.520
Your research here is being leaked to the M.H.R.R.?

00:18:07.520 --> 00:18:09.280
It is not being leaked.

00:18:09.280 --> 00:18:10.690
We are officially sending it to them.

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:13.360
The apocalypse is the whole world's problem.

00:18:13.360 --> 00:18:17.910
Even Catholic countries allied with the Testament Union are currently sending us reports.

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:21.370
Now do you understand the meaning of Avalon?

00:18:21.370 --> 00:18:25.000
We are working to resolve the apocalypse.

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:30.710
That is the same for M.H.R.R., K.P.A. Italia and even Tres España.

00:18:31.090 --> 00:18:34.470
Musashi is climbing up to join our ranks.

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:37.970
I suppose I should say, "I'm glad we came to England".

00:18:37.970 --> 00:18:40.220
I'd be upset if you didn't.

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:43.100
I've shown you the secret of my past.

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:46.100
I-It-It-It's horrible, your Majesty!

00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:48.270
Has something happened?

00:18:49.150 --> 00:18:52.190
Th-The moron is after Excalibur Caliburn!

00:18:52.190 --> 00:18:55.110
Wishing for health and a whole lot of happiness!

00:18:55.490 --> 00:18:58.080
I can't pull it out! I can't draw Excalibur!

00:18:58.080 --> 00:19:00.040
Why is this so thrilling?

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:04.080
Okay, that's it for today's practice.

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:05.710
I'll try for real tomorrow.

00:19:05.710 --> 00:19:07.250
There won't be a second time!

00:19:07.250 --> 00:19:08.500
Can you hear me?!

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:11.510
Lemme tell ya something cool!

00:19:11.510 --> 00:19:14.220
My nickname is "Impossible".

00:19:14.590 --> 00:19:17.760
So it's totally dead on that I couldn't draw Excalibur Caliburn!

00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:20.640
But someone aside from me,

00:19:20.640 --> 00:19:23.480
one of my buddies, will definitely draw this sword!

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:26.600
Tori!

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:28.650
Aw, crap!

00:19:28.650 --> 00:19:30.150
Hurry and scurry away!

00:19:32.530 --> 00:19:34.490
<i>But that is probably impossible...</i>

00:19:34.490 --> 00:19:37.110
<i>No one can draw Excalibur Caliburn</i>

00:19:37.110 --> 00:19:39.030
<i>and I will never get to see it be drawn.</i>

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:47.580
Ninja can be surprisingly helpful.

00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:50.920
He's working part-time for the
Engineering Club after getting dumped?

00:19:51.420 --> 00:19:53.840
I can't understand the workings of men's minds.

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:56.930
What brought a knight such as yourself here?

00:19:57.380 --> 00:19:59.550
I came to ask if we could train.

00:20:00.100 --> 00:20:03.180
Does it bug you that the Trump's hound bested you?

00:20:03.180 --> 00:20:04.060
Judge.

00:20:04.520 --> 00:20:06.480
How does Jizuri Suzaku look?

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:08.310
Not too good.

00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:12.020
I've been asking IZUMO's main branch to dispatch a repair specialist, but...

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:16.150
That's precisely why I'm here, Masa!

00:20:16.150 --> 00:20:18.450
Of all the people, they had to send you?

00:20:18.450 --> 00:20:19.820
Hey, hey, hey!

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:21.280
Did you really have to say it like that?

00:20:21.280 --> 00:20:22.620
Who is this?

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:25.870
Mishina Hiro, Old Man Taizo's granddaughter.

00:20:28.670 --> 00:20:29.620
Nice to meet ya!

00:20:29.960 --> 00:20:32.790
How dare you call me "We"?!

00:20:33.170 --> 00:20:34.800
I am truly sorry.
Vice Principal Yoshinao?

00:20:34.800 --> 00:20:36.760
And what is the Chancellor doing here?
I am truly sorry.

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:39.510
He asked us to let him hide down here a minute ago.

00:20:39.510 --> 00:20:43.350
We swear, your class has yet to learn a thing called manners!

00:20:44.390 --> 00:20:45.810
What could this be?

00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:49.850
Isn't this a map of England?

00:20:51.100 --> 00:20:54.270
And it leads to Oxford Academy in London...

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:57.690
Tenzo, are you going to attack the Tower of London?!

00:20:58.740 --> 00:21:01.660
<i>Don't shout out something that could become an international problem!</i>

00:21:01.660 --> 00:21:03.620
This is bad, isn't it, Your Majesty?

00:21:03.620 --> 00:21:07.450
This ninja plans to use the same trick as when he was fixing up the cemetery

00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:09.120
to stick Excalibur Caliburn between his legs!

00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:10.960
I would do no such thing!

00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:11.960
Goodness!

00:21:11.960 --> 00:21:15.460
Does that make this a tactical map for a date, Tenzo?

00:21:16.090 --> 00:21:16.550
Huh?

00:21:16.550 --> 00:21:19.470
These X's don't mark where the soldiers on guard duty stand.

00:21:19.470 --> 00:21:21.800
They represent high-end booths, don't they?!

00:21:22.050 --> 00:21:23.430
J-Judge.

00:21:24.640 --> 00:21:26.810
Then We shall offer you some advice.

00:21:27.350 --> 00:21:29.060
Here and here.

00:21:29.060 --> 00:21:31.850
There is also another station here.

00:21:32.270 --> 00:21:33.310
Sir...

00:21:33.690 --> 00:21:37.610
If you are going, go with pride, but remember to be stealthy.

00:21:37.610 --> 00:21:39.570
That is the trick behind sneaking a date.

00:21:41.030 --> 00:21:43.070
Are you seriously going on a date, Tenzo?

00:21:43.570 --> 00:21:44.830
No, well...

00:21:45.620 --> 00:21:47.620
Huh? That scar!

00:21:49.160 --> 00:21:51.370
Didn't Scarred heal that for you?

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:52.170
Judge.

00:21:52.170 --> 00:21:54.670
But she left a scar on you, Tenzo.

00:21:56.590 --> 00:21:58.340
But if I fell for someone,

00:21:58.340 --> 00:22:01.970
I would like to be the type of woman who can give him a scar

00:22:01.970 --> 00:22:03.260
that lasts a lifetime.

00:22:03.760 --> 00:22:05.760
She left a scar...

00:22:06.140 --> 00:22:08.100
Hey, whatcha thinking, Tenzo?

00:22:08.600 --> 00:22:09.470
Sir Tori!

00:22:09.770 --> 00:22:11.230
Yeah? What is it?

00:22:11.640 --> 00:22:13.730
On the final day of the festival,

00:22:14.980 --> 00:22:17.730
I will probably make a big announcement.

00:22:18.150 --> 00:22:20.320
I just remembered I had a mission to do.

00:22:21.030 --> 00:22:21.820
Sorry!

00:22:42.260 --> 00:22:43.880
<i>Wait for me,</i>

00:22:44.630 --> 00:22:45.800
<i>Master Scarred!</i>
